{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>YHWH is a man of war.</b> That is, even with the attribute of mercy He waged war, and He did not change because of this, heaven forbid, but rather ״YHWH is His name״ — in the manner of (Malachi 3:6) ״אֲנִי ה׳ לֹא שָׁנִיתִי״. Or it may intend that at the very time He waged war against the Egyptians, at that very time He was conducting Himself with the attribute of mercy toward Israel, as I explained in connection with His blessed statement (Exodus 6:2) ״וַיְדַבֵּר אֱלֹהִים אֶל מֹשֶׁה וְגוֹ׳ אֲנִי ה׳״."], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:28:17.102668594Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}